/-!
# The congruence subgroup of an *ideal* modulus, and the associated principal ray

`Submission/Work/.../IdealModulus/Defs.lean` introduces the vocabulary `DvdPrime`, `FracCoprimeId`,
`CongrOneId`, `principalRayId`, `idealCoprimeGroupId`, `normRayId`, `IsAdmissibleId`,
`ContainsRamified` for an ideal modulus `𝔪 : Ideal (𝓞 K)`.

This file adds the *idèlic* side of the dictionary:

* `CongrAtId 𝔭 𝔪 y` — the local congruence `y ≡ 1 mod 𝔪` at `𝔭` (at the level
  `count K 𝔭 𝔪`), the ideal-modulus analogue of `NK.CFTLib.Arl.CongrAt`;
* `congruenceSubgroupId K 𝔪` — the congruence subgroup `U(𝔪) ≤ 𝕀 K` of idèles congruent to `1`
  modulo `𝔪` at the primes `𝔭 | 𝔪` and positive at every real place, the analogue of
  `NK.CFTLib.Arl.congruenceSubgroup`;
* `principalRayClId K 𝔪` — the classical principal ray `P(𝔪)`, the image of the principal idèles
  of `U(𝔪)` in the group of fractional ideals, the analogue of `NK.CFTLib.ARL.principalRay`.

Note the difference between `principalRayId 𝔪` (the subgroup generated by the principal ideals
`(a)` with `a - 1 ∈ 𝔪`, i.e. `a ≡ 1` at *every* prime) and `principalRayClId 𝔪` (the subgroup
generated by the principal ideals `(a)` with `a ≡ 1 mod 𝔪` at the primes dividing `𝔪` only).
The two subgroups are nevertheless *equal*, see `principalRayClId_le_principalRayId`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false
set_option linter.style.haveILetI false
set_option maxHeartbeats 800000

open scoped NumberField nonZeroDivisors
open NumberField IsDedekindDomain

